<title>TURKEY: Turkish Osmanli Bank gets $50-mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Osmanli Bank gets $50-mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Osmanli Bankasi signed an accord on Wednesday for a $50 million syndicated loan, the Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>The one-year pre-export financing facility carried an interest of 50 basis points over LIBOR, it said.</p>
<p>Eleven banks, including American Express, Bank of New York, Bayerische Vereinsbank, National Westminister, Barclays, Royal Bank of Canada and Standard Chartered, participated in the deal.</p>
</text>
